<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain has no comment on rate-checking talk.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain has no comment on rate-checking talk.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain declined to comment, as is its custom, on talk it had been checking peseta/mark exchange rates.</p>
<p>Dealers said the bank was checking prices at 84.10 per mark, but the central bank had no comment.</p>
<p>At 1225 GMT, the peseta was trading at 84.10/11 per mark.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
